  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math><msub><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><msub><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> be the number of red and black balls, respectively, in box I. Let <math><msub><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><msub><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub></math> be the number of red and black balls, respectively, in box II.<br />A ball is drawn at random from box I and transferred to box II. If the probability of drawing a red ball from box I, after this transfer, is <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> , then the correct options(s) with the possible values of <math><msub><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><msub><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> is(are)"
